# UI changes require approval

Before changing anything visible to the user (layout, labels, icons, colors, spacing, new controls, copy, tooltips, animations):

1. **Describe** what you plan to change and why (brief bullet list).
2. **Wait** for explicit user approval — do not implement UI tweaks “to help” or for discoverability without consent.
3. **Default** to matching existing toolbar/panel patterns (icon-only buttons, same sizes as neighbors, no extra text labels unless requested).
4. **Functional fixes** (bugs, crashes, missing wiring) may proceed without a UI design review, but must not add new visual elements beyond what the approved spec requires.

If the user only asked for backend/logic work, do not change UI at all unless required for the task.
